raising edge keep this competitive"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to Democrats in an open, near-even district during a favorable midterm environment, and most expert raters plus prediction markets lean toward Amish Shah. Jay Feely's cash advantage and recent damaging stories about Shah temper the outlook, so the forecast sits slightly below the consensus of ratings.", "watch": "Any general-election polling or a shift in the national environment could move this; a Tossup reading from Inside Elections and Sabato shows the range of outcomes if Feely closes the money gap.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: David Schweikert (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Arizona's 1st District is an open seat with Republican David Schweikert leaving to run for governor. State Rep. Amish Shah, who upset the Democratic establishment in the primary, faces former NFL kicker Jay Feely, with Libertarian Monica Alponte also on the ballot. The district sits near even partisanship, so the national midterm environment matters heavily.\n\nMost expert raters place the race at Lean Democratic for a flip, though Inside Elections and Sabato's Crystal Ball call it a Tossup. Prediction markets give Shah roughly a 76-82% chance. Feely has outraised Shah and faces no outside opposition spending, while Shah carries heavy outside spending against him and recent negative coverage. The race remains competitive but tilts Democratic.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7982, "margin": 5.27}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7812, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7872, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7849, "margin": 5.0}]}